sentences.l:
So then having spoken, he sat down, and Telemachus
having thrown his arms round his good father wailed, tears pouring,
and in the two of them alike there rose up beneath a longing for lament;

and they wept clearly, more heavily than birds,
sea-eagles or crook-taloned vultures, whose young
countrymen have taken out before they could become winged;

But for us two alone two swords and two spears
to leave behind, and two ox-hide shields to take in our hands,
so that, rushing in, we may seize them;

let no one then of Odysseus hear that he is within,
neither Laertes know that, nor the swineherd,
nor any of the household, nor Penelope herself,
but alone, you and I, of the women let us learn the inclination;
